{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"alias":"uncivil-flavoury-mantisray","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Intake deduplication is keyed on a ticket content digest that the platform's own write-backs mutate, so a ticket that has already been worked becomes re-admittable and starts a duplicate run.\n\nThe intake ledger records a SideEffectRef with operation intake_start and target built from the content digest and the repository. The platform writes back to the ticket during a run, adding comments and status changes, which changes the ticket content and therefore the digest. A later poll computes a different target, finds no matching ledger entry, and admits the ticket again. The active execution guard is the only thing preventing the duplicate, so the moment an execution row reaches a terminal state the ticket is eligible to run again.\n\nObserved when intake admitted a duplicate run for ticket 53ed-ac2d-7739-4194 after its first run had already produced a pull request. The duplicate was intake-8383b6ac and was terminated manually at PLANNING.\n\nThe fix should key deduplication on ticket identity rather than on mutable content, while still allowing a deliberate re-run when an operator asks for one. Investigate how a re-run is meant to be requested before choosing the key, since the watermark poller currently relies on content changing to surface a ticket at all.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Intake deduplication is keyed on a value that the platform's own write-backs do not change\n- [ ] A ticket that has already produced a run is not admitted again by an unrelated content change\n- [ ] A deliberate operator requested re-run is still admitted\n- [ ] The watermark poller still surfaces a ticket that has never been run\n\n## Testing\nAdd unit tests under tests/unit covering the deduplication key and the re-run path, then run `pytest tests/unit -q` and `ruff check .`.","id":"1473-be1f-bfde-4146","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["intake","idempotency"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Key intake deduplication on ticket identity rather than mutable content"},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789965180250522001,"uuid":"da973629-2e4a-4f4c-bb5c-286a7fc5c90a"}